monster_from:
ZzzCharacter.cpp:14034-14039, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_ELITE_YETI:

    OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_ELITE_YETI);
    c = CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_ELITE_YETI, PositionX, PositionY);
    wcscpy(c->ID, L"설인 대장");
    c->Object.Scale = 1.4f;

No weapon, no BlendMesh, no HiddenMesh, no Level. At 1.4 the 164-unit model stands about 2.3 m.

effects_from:
MoveCharacterVisual's per-frame switch, ZzzCharacter.cpp:6181-6189:

    case MODEL_YETI:
    case MODEL_ELITE_YETI:
        if (rand_fps_check(4))
        {
            Vector(0.f, 0.f, 0.f, p);
            b->TransformPosition(o->BoneTransform[22], p, Position, true);
            CreateParticle(BITMAP_SMOKE, Position, o->Angle, o->Light);
        }
        break;

Its breath in the cold: one BITMAP_SMOKE a fourth of the reference frames on average, at bone 22 itself (Box03, the muzzle), in every action -- idle, walk, fight and fall; no clip window, unlike the Bull Fighter's. BITMAP_SMOKE with no subtype is the Bull Fighter's snort particle exactly (ZzzEffectParticle.cpp:1145-1160 birth, :5271-5278 motion: 16 frames, scale 0.48-0.80 growing 0.05 a frame, rising on a Gravity growing 0.2 a frame, Luminosity = LifeTime / 8), which src/game/fx/snort.h already draws.

The plain Yeti's snowball (ZzzCharacter.cpp:5125-5128, `if (o->Type == MODEL_YETI) CreateEffect(MODEL_SNOW1, ...)`) is the plain one's alone; the Elite has no missile and no AttackSkill. It bleeds as anything else does (CreateBlood's ordinary branch, ZzzEffectBlurSpark.cpp:456-467).
